WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.150
Point a telescope at a distant galaxy
and spread its light out by wavelength.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.160
You find familiar dark lines, the same
pattern measured in the laboratory.

3
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.200
But every line sits at
a longer wavelength.

4
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.910
The whole pattern has shifted together.

5
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.960
Almost every distant galaxy shows this.

6
00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:23.710
So how fast is a galaxy moving away,
to stretch its light like that?

7
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.280
In this mission, you'll turn
a measured shift into a speed,

8
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.990
step by step.

9
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.750
Then you'll find out what the
shifts tell us about the universe.

10
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.640
Your mission: calculate how fast a galaxy
is moving away from the stretch in its

11
00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:38.270
light.
